  "facts": [
    "The Bayonne Bridge, completed in 1931, was the world’s longest through‑arch bridge at the time, outlasting the Sydney Harbour Bridge by 25 feet and weighing a mere 16,000 short tons.",
    "Designed by Swiss engineer Othmar Ammann and architect Cass Gilbert, the bridge’s 40‑segment steel arch rises 266 feet above the Kill Van Kull, a feat achieved without blocking shipping traffic.",
    "A 2013‑2019 Port Authority project raised the bridge’s clearance 64 feet, from 151 to 215 feet, enabling Post‑Panamax ships to pass beneath while adding a new roadway and pedestrian path."
